<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danishnama-yi Ala'i</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1030</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Danishnama</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Danishnama-yi Ala'i, &quot;Book of Knowledge for Ala al-Dawla&quot;, is a philosophical encyclopaedia written in Persian by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avicenna">Ibn Sina</a> (Avicenna) at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a> for his patron, the Kakuyid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-al-dawla-muhammad">Ala al-Dawla Muhammad</a>. Covering logic, metaphysics and natural science, it is among the earliest works of philosophy written in Persian rather than Arabic.</p></div>
